  "summary": "Clear key and value DataStream buffers in BerkeleyROCursor::Next() before copying the next record into them. This aligns the Berkeley DB read-only cursor with SQLiteCursor and documents the replacement contract on DatabaseCursor::Next().",
  "problem": "During legacy wallet migration (migratewallet), record deserializers can leave optional suffix bytes unread, such as extra flag bytes in v2 key metadata. Because LoadRecords reuses the same stream instances across records and BerkeleyROCursor::Next() appends to them without clearing, leftover bytes pollute the deserialization of subsequent records and cause migration to fail with corruption errors.",
  "evidence": [
    "The PR description notes that migratewallet rejects valid legacy wallets as corrupt when v2 key metadata includes trailing unread flag bytes, and the included regression test fails without the fix."
  ],
