  "card": "Clears key and value stream buffers in BerkeleyROCursor::Next() before copying each record, matching SQLiteCursor. Currently, LoadRecords reuses stream objects across records, causing unread suffix bytes from one record to contaminate subsequent records and fail legacy wallet migrations with false corruption errors. The author demonstrates this bug on old wallets with unread v2 metadata bytes, and regression coverage confirms the cursor now properly replaces stream contents. The PR has no dependencies.",
